1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,560
Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,320
<i>If you make one shot out of five,</i>
<i>I'll let you be my roommate.</i>

3
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,680
Did it go in?

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,720
It did.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:17,800
Yo, my roommate!

6
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:20,040
But you have to promise me something.

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:24,280
If anything unlucky happens,
you have to move out right away.

8
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:25,800
Okay.

9
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,480
- Deal!
- Deal!

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,320
My name is Khobfa.

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:39,360
I am eight years old.

12
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:46,320
I like to eat fried rice,

13
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,200
and I want…

14
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:57,800
to help my fa…

15
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,480
…ter.

16
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,120
Okay.

17
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,640
It's fine, sweetheart.

18
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:18,640
"Father."

19
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:20,600
Try pronouncing it. "Father."

20
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,560
Father.

21
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,560
Okay. Make sure to pronounce it correctly
before helping your father.

22
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:26,960
Got it, sweetheart?

23
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:37,280
<i>Keep this in mind, students. We're Thai.</i>

24
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,920
We should be brave to speak English.

25
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:11,600
Come on.

26
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,600
- Ouch.
- Here. I'll help you.

27
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,680
Man, you're really going all out.

28
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,480
Going all out for what?

29
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,520
Moving in with a tough guy like Khobfa.

30
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,520
What do you mean?

31
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,080
We know what you're trying to do.

32
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,680
You're trying to get back at Krit, right?

33
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,120
Nice one, bro. That's smart.

34
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,640
Actually, I--

35
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,800
It's fine, Rin.

36
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,160
You're still our friend. I'm cool with it.

37
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:47,120
But if Khobfa finds out about your plan
and does anything bad to you,

38
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,640
tell us right away.

39
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,400
Yeah, Rin. You have to tell us right away.

40
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,200
But this is the right move.
Revenge has to be served.

41
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,960
You're seriously smart.

42
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,560
You're an amazing friend.

43
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,160
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

44
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,880
Yeah. Let's do this.

45
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,320
<i>I'm here. What are you doing?</i>

46
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:25,600
GIVE ME A SEC. I JUST WOKE UP.

47
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:29,000
Guys, I feel like
I'm forgetting something.

48
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:32,040
Should we take a selfie for my story?

49
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:33,400
- Sure.
- Yeah?

50
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,200
Sending our friend into a guy's room
for the first time!

51
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,080
What do you mean by that?

52
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,640
Stop complaining and take the picture.

53
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:41,960
Ready?

54
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,680
Three, two, one.

55
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,080
Well…

56
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:59,480
This is Ohm, and this is Jinnie.

57
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:01,600
My friends.

58
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,000
Yeah.

59
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:06,200
Can I ask you something?

60
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,720
Why did your landlord
ask for the house back?

61
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,640
- We wrecked it.
- The owner sold the property.

62
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:18,720
Huh?

63
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,880
- The owner sold the property.
- We wrecked the house…

64
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:25,640
- Well… The pipes broke, right?
- Well…

65
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:29,000
Well, the landlord's renovating the place.

66
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,280
- Yeah. Right.
- Right. Renovating.

67
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,840
- And property prices have gone up too.
- Right.

68
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,480
So we had to hurry and move out.

69
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,000
- It was exhausting.
- Yeah.

70
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,200
I'm still not done packing.

71
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,680
Me neither.

72
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,960
All right, good luck. See you later.

73
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,040
See you later.

74
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,120
Should I bring my stuff in now?

75
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:11,200
So, what are your roommate rules?

76
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,480
I can handle anything.

77
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,480
Don't move any
of my personal belongings, ever.

78
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,600
Yeah, sure.

79
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,280
Same goes for my stuff.

80
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,120
Don't touch them.

81
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:32,720
Fine.

82
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,000
What's next?

83
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,080
You're studying fine arts, right?

84
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,160
Yeah.

85
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,280
Don't get paint all over my room.

86
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,480
Easy. What else?

87
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:50,160
I'm a clean freak.
Don't make my room dirty. Got it?

88
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,160
Don't make the room dirty. Got it.

89
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,080
Yeah.

90
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,280
The bed is over there.

91
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,960
Wow.

92
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:17,800
So I sleep in the bed,
and you sleep down there, right?

93
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,640
That's cute.

94
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,200
Wait.

95
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,200
You've got it wrong.

96
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:28,520
You sleep down there. I sleep in the bed.

97
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,120
I think you said that wrong.

98
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,920
Who gets the bed? Say it again.

99
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:38,120
You sleep down there.

100
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,880
Got it?

101
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,600
Right.

102
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:49,960
Where's the bathroom?

103
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,960
Hang in there.

104
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,200
I can do this.

105
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:12,080
Once his birthday comes,
it'll all be over.

106
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,360
Shit!

107
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,760
What happened?

108
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:37,320
Who told you
to leave your boxers lying here, idiot?

109
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,960
I'm giving you one week.
You can stay here--

110
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,960
"But nothing unlucky
can happen because of you."

111
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:07,920
If anything bad happens to me,
I'm leaving this room right away.

112
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:11,360
You've said that five times already.
I remember.

113
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,480
I'm keeping my eye on you.

114
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,000
I'm the one keeping an eye on you.

115
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,720
No, I'm keeping my eye on you.

116
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,160
I'm keeping my eye on you.

117
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,560
I'm keeping my eye on you.

118
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,480
Me.

119
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,560
- No, me.
- I'm keeping an eye on you.

120
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,120
- Me.
- I'm the one watching you.

121
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:44,600
<i>I'm his roommate now. I'll try my best</i>
<i>to stay with him until his birthday.</i>

122
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,920
<i>Then you can stop worrying now.</i>

123
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,240
Khobfa.

124
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:01,480
Hey. Nothing unlucky
happened to you today, right?

125
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,840
Is that how you say hello?

126
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,840
Stand farther away.

127
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,560
So what's the plan?

128
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,440
We've been waiting forever.

129
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,720
Let's go inside.

130
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:58,840
You two always arrive together these days.

131
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,600
We're roommates.
Of course we arrive together.

132
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:05,240
Right?

133
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:09,720
Yeah.

134
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,560
So I guess we're condo buddies now.

135
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,280
Why are you going this far, Rin?

136
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,040
What do you mean?

137
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,800
All of this.

138
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:37,840
Why do you have to go this far?

139
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,240
How far is "this far"?

140
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,880
As far as what you did to me?

141
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:48,120
Seriously, Krit.
You have no right to say that to me.

142
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,720
I'm only asking

143
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,800
because I'm worried about you.

144
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,040
<i>It's over.</i>

145
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:03,720
<i>No matter what you do,</i>

146
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,160
we're already over.

147
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,160
You said things between you were over,

148
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:23,240
so make sure they really are.

149
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,840
Just leave me here.

150
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,120
Okay.

151
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:08,560
Take care of yourself.

152
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,400
Yeah.

153
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,760
TOP 5 FINALISTS

154
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:31,840
If you're going to do this,
it should be more evenly matched.

155
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,680
What are you talking about?

156
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:39,280
Look at Khobfa.

157
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,120
I don't think
he can easily compete with Krit.

158
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,720
How do you know Khobfa can't beat Krit?

159
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:53,480
Just wait and see whether Krit or Khobfa
will be the one who wins.

160
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:55,800
Fine.

161
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,440
Is your pitching presentation ready?

162
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,560
I'm waiting to coach you.

163
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,640
I just told the professor I'm withdrawing.

164
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:17,760
What?

165
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:21,120
Why would you withdraw?

166
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:24,280
What are you so scared of?

167
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:26,640
I can help you beat Krit.

168
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:30,520
Why do I have to beat Krit?

169
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:34,920
What? Don't you want to beat someone
who looked down on you?

170
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,400
You're always like this.

171
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,640
You just let people look down on you.

172
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,120
You don't know anything.

173
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,080
Can you stay out of it?

174
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,680
Seriously?

175
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:02,160
Why did Khobfa withdraw?

176
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,000
I'm not sure.

177
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:06,360
Well, that's good.

178
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,800
Just do your best.

179
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,160
I'm sure you can win
the championship again.

180
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:14,280
Honestly, I'm still not that confident.

181
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:18,920
The last time I won,
it was partly because of Rin.

182
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:23,200
Hey, you can stand on your own now.

183
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:26,480
You're really good.
Believe in yourself more.

184
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:32,480
Show Rin that you can do
just fine without him.

185
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:36,360
If I win,

186
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,120
do I get a reward?

187
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:41,280
What do you want?

188
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,360
My…

189
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:52,000
foot or my fist?

190
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:56,480
Come on, Mochi. That's not very creative.

191
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,200
I'm kidding.

192
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,120
Fine. I'll treat you…

193
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,480
I'll treat you to an omakase.

194
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:09,760
Oh, really? Wow, thank you so much.

195
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,400
<i>I'm working on it as fast as I can.</i>
<i>Prof. James isn't going to yell at me.</i>

196
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:17,800
<i>How are you doing?</i>
<i>How's your roommate? Is he okay?</i>

197
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:24,960
I guess.

198
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:29,640
I was talking to him just fine,
but then he turned his ass toward me.

199
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,160
Stop playing already.

200
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:41,240
Why? You can't handle it?

201
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:47,400
If you can't, go stay somewhere else.
You don't have to be my roommate.

202
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Seriously, you…

203
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:57,080
Try talking back to other people
the way you do to me.

204
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,319
Khobfa!

205
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,680
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

206
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:00,680
I'm sorry.

207
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,920
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

208
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,760
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

209
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,840
I didn't do it.

210
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:12,440
I'm a jinx, aren't I?

211
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,800
I'm the reason Mom and Dad died.

212
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:41,640
I'm sorry I'm a jinx.

213
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,880
<i>I'm sorry, Dad.</i>

214
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:37,320
<i>I don't think I can do it.</i>

215
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,080
Why did you mess with my stuff?

216
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:43,640
If we ignore the grammar
and add a little more sincerity,

217
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:46,200
I think this is already pretty good,

218
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:51,360
especially the part inspired by your dad.

219
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:57,040
You should stay in the competition.

220
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:01,440
But I'm not good at English.

221
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:04,520
I got made fun of for it as a kid.

222
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:19,600
You can always practice a language.

223
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,400
But what's in here…

224
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:31,400
and in here…

225
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:35,560
I think they're already amazing.

226
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,560
You don't need to practice them.

227
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,560
Just stay in the competition.

228
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:47,080
Don't do it for anyone else.

229
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,120
Just go up there

230
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:03,320
and imagine you're telling your dad
about your project.

231
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:16,600
Let me help you.

232
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:21,480
Consider it part of me
being your roommate.

233
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:23,520
Let me do something for you.

234
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:28,840
Please? Come on. Please.

235
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:36,160
Please. I'm begging you.

236
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,320
Please let me help you.

237
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,520
Fine. Okay. Let's do it.

238
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,240
Yay!

239
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:52,720
I'll help you, so don't worry.
I'm going to train you hard, okay?

240
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:55,440
I'll turn you into
a top businessman in this country.

241
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:58,800
I guarantee your pitch will be amazing.

242
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:09,800
"My project is helping people
to can have a house."

243
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:12,560
Hey. You can't say "to can."

244
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,840
Then what am I supposed to say?

245
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:19,920
This part should be,
"helps people own a house."

246
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,920
"And asset owners unlock the hidden value
of what they already have."

247
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,480
"This is not just a smarter way to spend."

248
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:29,160
"It's a smarter way to live. Thank you."

249
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,160
Was it okay?

250
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,320
I think…

251
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:35,600
It was okay.

252
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:37,880
<i>Okay.</i>

253
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:41,080
"My project is help people own house

254
00:25:41,760 --> 00:25:46,120
because my father, he working very hard,
but still don't have a house."

255
00:25:46,840 --> 00:25:47,680
Wrong.

256
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:49,440
You just need to smile a little more.

257
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:52,160
Smile often. You look cute when you smile.

258
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:59,360
"He works very hard
but still doesn't have a house."

259
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,360
That's better.

260
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:01,360
Yes!

261
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:04,360
Now, when you speak,
you have to speak from the heart.

262
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:07,520
You have to feel it, okay?

263
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:09,920
<i>How do I smile?</i>

264
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:13,280
Well, smile like this.

265
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,280
Do I look cute now?

266
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,240
Do you think I can do it?

267
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:44,840
You really like competitions, don't you?

268
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:46,880
They're challenging.

269
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:51,400
And maybe my family
will finally be proud of me.

270
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:03,840
I believe your family
will be proud of what you do.

271
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:09,200
Just like I've always been proud of you.

272
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:18,520
You're proud of me?

273
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:22,280
I guess.

274
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:24,280
I don't know.

275
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:26,680
Well, if you win,

276
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:29,280
then Rin can stop using Khobfa
to make you jealous.

277
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:36,160
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

278
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:37,120
I'm sorry.

279
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:39,600
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

280
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:41,880
Stop talking to your grandson like that.

281
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:43,920
He didn't do anything wrong.

282
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,040
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA
MAR 6,1980-JAN 12, 2020

283
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:47,640
Khobfa, sweetheart.

284
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:49,640
Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?

285
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:50,640
Stop it!

286
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:52,600
I didn't want this to happen.

287
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:56,600
I'm sorry.

288
00:27:58,640 --> 00:27:59,720
I didn't mean to.

289
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:03,880
I didn't want any of this to happen.

290
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,440
Here.

291
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:27,400
You didn't sleep well last night?

292
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:29,520
Yeah.

293
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:32,160
I've been having bad dreams lately.

294
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:35,840
Want me to take you to campus?

295
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:41,160
No need.
Don't you have an afternoon class?

296
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:45,520
But how will you get there?
You'll drive when you're this sleepy?

297
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:48,680
That's my problem.

298
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:31,560
What happened to Khobfa?

299
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,920
He probably got into trouble again.

300
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,800
When is Ohm getting here?

301
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,600
- We've been waiting forever.
- Yeah.

302
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:42,720
Rin, Jinnie!

303
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:45,120
- Look at this.
- Huh?

304
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,960
What the hell did Khobfa do?

305
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:49,480
Everyone's sharing it.

306
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:51,880
They're saying that thug
got into another fight.

307
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:54,280
He looks like
he got into a fight with a dog.

308
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,320
Your roommate…

309
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,440
Be careful around him.

310
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:02,720
Let me see.

311
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:07,760
Look at him.

312
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:11,120
<i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>cannot be reached at this time.</i>

313
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,200
<i>Please leave your message.</i>

314
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:17,960
- What?
- Hey!

315
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:44,920
Where are you, Khobfa?

316
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:48,640
Are you looking for me?

317
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,360
Khobfa!

318
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:56,560
What happened to you?

319
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:00,640
I just fell off my motorbike this morning.

320
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,560
I told you. If you're sleepy, don't drive.

321
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:09,280
I just didn't get enough sleep.
I only blacked out for a second.

322
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:10,920
It wasn't because of bad luck.

323
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:22,000
Can you please stop getting yourself hurt?

324
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,480
<i>What should I do?</i>
<i>His bad luck is starting again.</i>

325
00:31:39,080 --> 00:31:42,000
<i>He's been having nightmares so often</i>
<i>that he doesn't get enough sleep.</i>

326
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:43,680
<i>Then he rode his motorbike and crashed.</i>

327
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,200
<i>Easy, kid.</i>

328
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:49,960
<i>Maybe he's not unlucky.</i>
<i>Maybe he's just sleep-deprived.</i>

329
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:54,560
<i>Exactly.</i>

330
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:57,800
<i>Nothing beats a good night's sleep</i>
<i>and sweet dreams.</i>

331
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:07,200
What are you making?

332
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:12,880
A dreamcatcher.
They're really trendy right now.

333
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:14,800
What's that?

334
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:17,440
Self-care is really trendy these days.

335
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:19,800
If you're going to be healthy,
go all the way,

336
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:22,560
both when you're awake
and when you're asleep.

337
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:27,320
Basically, the web catches the bad dreams

338
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:31,520
and lets the good dreams pass through,
so you can sleep peacefully.

339
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,440
Seriously?

340
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,680
Of course.

341
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:40,360
Wait, you're wearing one too.

342
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:42,440
You don't know what it means?

343
00:32:44,160 --> 00:32:48,320
No. My mom gave it to me,
but I never knew what it meant.

344
00:32:57,880 --> 00:33:01,560
<i>Nothing beats a good night's sleep</i>
<i>and sweet dreams.</i>

345
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:18,080
Ouch.

346
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:24,080
Why is it so tight?

347
00:33:39,360 --> 00:33:40,200
Ouch.

348
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:03,160
I hope this helps you, Khobfa.

349
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:14,600
Hey, what are you doing?

350
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:20,560
I thought it looked nice, so I was
going to decorate the room with it.

351
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:28,280
No. If you want to hang that up,
hang it on your side.

352
00:34:29,719 --> 00:34:33,520
Come on. Something like this
looks best by the window.

353
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:36,000
But this is my side. I don't like it.

354
00:34:37,320 --> 00:34:39,360
Just leave it. You'll like it eventually.

355
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:42,040
Why are you forcing me?

356
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:44,120
Did you forget this is my room?

357
00:34:45,080 --> 00:34:46,760
Stop messing with my stuff.

358
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:56,560
Hey, but this can stop your nightmares.

359
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,440
It's called a dreamcatcher.

360
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:10,840
You've been having nightmares
and not getting enough sleep.

361
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:13,440
I just wanted to help you.

362
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:21,800
I don't want it. I'm fine.

363
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:45,720
Rin, can we talk?

364
00:35:47,600 --> 00:35:48,600
What is it?

365
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:53,480
I know I don't have the right
to tell you who you can date.

366
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:58,040
But if you're going to date someone,
can't you choose someone better?

367
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:03,480
What do you mean?

368
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:11,160
Didn't you tell me yourself
to stay away from Khobfa?

369
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:13,920
So what's this?
You're getting close to him now.

370
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:18,640
Nobody wants Khobfa.
He's nothing but bad luck.

371
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:20,280
Krit.

372
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:22,800
I never thought
you'd be this kind of person.

373
00:36:23,400 --> 00:36:26,080
I don't care
what other people say about Khobfa.

374
00:36:26,640 --> 00:36:30,360
The Khobfa I know
is nothing like what they say.

375
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:05,000
Here.

376
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:06,720
I got this for you.

377
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:22,640
Why are you waiting for me
in front of my faculty?

378
00:37:25,600 --> 00:37:28,080
We're supposed to practice
our presentation today.

379
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:37,360
Thanks…

380
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:43,720
for standing up for me like that.

381
00:37:44,320 --> 00:37:45,480
You heard that?

382
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:52,840
People just say whatever they want.

383
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:55,040
I felt uncomfortable
hearing them talk like that.

384
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:01,920
I'm sorry.

385
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:05,440
I might've made you
uncomfortable yesterday too.

386
00:38:08,040 --> 00:38:10,000
Maybe I really am what they say I am.

387
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:12,560
I don't think so.

388
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:19,280
Come on.

389
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:22,080
Let's practice the presentation
and prove them wrong.

390
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:43,920
Okay. Today, we're practicing
without a script.

391
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:46,600
It'll be like
you're actually onstage. Okay?

392
00:38:47,240 --> 00:38:51,640
Then imagine
I'm a top businessman in the country,

393
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:54,080
looking for a new business to invest in.

394
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:56,320
Whenever you're ready, the floor is yours.

395
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:09,560
My… name is…

396
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:20,720
<i>Keep this in mind, students. We're Thai.</i>

397
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:22,920
We should be brave to speak English.

398
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:26,240
My name…

399
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:29,520
What's wrong?

400
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:31,760
I'm not used to this!

401
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:38,240
I had to present in front of the class
when I was a kid.

402
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:41,680
I said something wrong,
and my teacher laughed at me.

403
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:45,760
I can't do it.
I can't speak in front of people!

404
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:55,720
So what did that teacher look like?

405
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:31,800
What was her name?

406
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:34,000
Teacher Maratee.

407
00:40:35,160 --> 00:40:36,640
Teacher Maratee.

408
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:40,000
With all due respect,
what kind of teacher are you?

409
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:43,040
Just because a kid can't speak English
in front of the class,

410
00:40:43,120 --> 00:40:44,600
that doesn't mean he's stupid.

411
00:40:45,120 --> 00:40:48,400
Wait. You're the one teaching him, right?

412
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:51,840
So maybe the problem is
you didn't teach him properly.

413
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:53,520
And another thing.

414
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:56,680
Making a kid stand there
while everyone laughs at them isn't right.

415
00:40:57,960 --> 00:41:00,040
Come on. Your turn.

416
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:01,640
Huh?

417
00:41:02,920 --> 00:41:04,080
Scold her.

418
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:10,000
Yeah.

419
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,480
You shouldn't do that.

420
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:17,200
Come on, harsher than that.

421
00:41:27,680 --> 00:41:28,800
Yeah!

422
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:31,240
You know some kids
aren't good at this subject,

423
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:32,960
but they're still trying their best.

424
00:41:33,040 --> 00:41:34,240
What kind of teacher are you?

425
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:37,240
Is making fun of your own student
hilarious to you or something?

426
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:48,480
Thanks.

427
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:51,200
I'll do my best.

428
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:54,120
I promise I won't let you down.

429
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:01,400
Don't do it for me.

430
00:42:02,040 --> 00:42:04,040
Don't worry about what anyone else says.

431
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:06,880
Just tell them what you want to tell them.

432
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:44,200
This platform lets people rent items
instead of buying them,

433
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:48,320
so they only pay
for what they actually use.

434
00:42:49,720 --> 00:42:50,880
At the same time,

435
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:54,840
the owners can earn from items
they already have but rarely use.

436
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:58,080
We simply connect both sides

437
00:42:58,680 --> 00:43:01,000
without holding inventory.

438
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:03,720
Students,
if you haven't finished your work,

439
00:43:03,800 --> 00:43:05,200
you're not going anywhere.

440
00:43:05,280 --> 00:43:07,200
It's just a simple landscape drawing.

441
00:43:07,760 --> 00:43:10,040
- Ohm, hurry up.
- Okay.

442
00:43:10,120 --> 00:43:14,320
So it turns unused assets
into real assets.

443
00:43:18,720 --> 00:43:20,920
This is not just a smarter way to spend.

444
00:43:23,120 --> 00:43:25,400
This is a smarter way to live.

445
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:28,280
Thank you.

446
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,160
<i>Look at Krit.</i>

447
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:38,400
He nailed the presentation.

448
00:43:40,160 --> 00:43:41,200
<i>Incredible!</i>

449
00:43:41,280 --> 00:43:43,440
Prof, can you just
finish the class already?

450
00:43:53,200 --> 00:43:54,520
You did amazing.

451
00:43:55,200 --> 00:44:02,200
All right. Next is the second contestant,
Mr. Watchiravit Kaoiam.

452
00:44:06,240 --> 00:44:07,520
You did very well today.

453
00:44:07,600 --> 00:44:09,880
Leave your work with your friend.
Collect and submit them.

454
00:44:09,960 --> 00:44:12,640
- See you, everyone. Thank you very much.
- Thank you. Goodbye.

455
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:13,760
Collect the assignments.

456
00:44:13,840 --> 00:44:16,360
Hey, can you pack my stuff for me?
I've got to go.

457
00:44:16,440 --> 00:44:17,760
- Go ahead.
- Hurry up.

458
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:20,040
Sending my support to Khobfa!

459
00:44:20,120 --> 00:44:21,840
Hurry up, dude!

460
00:44:32,840 --> 00:44:33,720
Khobfa.

461
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:38,560
- What are you doing here?
- Excuse me.

462
00:44:38,640 --> 00:44:40,360
- Be careful!
- Khobfa!

463
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:54,280
You almost got hurt.

464
00:44:54,920 --> 00:44:55,960
Thanks.

465
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:58,160
Are you ready?

466
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:08,040
I'm ready.

467
00:45:09,200 --> 00:45:10,400
Let's go.

468
00:45:11,040 --> 00:45:11,880
Let's go.

469
00:45:15,440 --> 00:45:16,400
Oops!

470
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:19,960
I'm sorry.

471
00:45:25,960 --> 00:45:27,560
- Shit!
- Shit!

472
00:45:44,600 --> 00:45:45,640
Take off your shirt.

473
00:45:45,720 --> 00:45:46,680
Huh?

474
00:45:46,760 --> 00:45:48,200
Just wear mine for now.

475
00:45:48,880 --> 00:45:49,800
Hurry.

476
00:46:02,720 --> 00:46:03,920
Let's switch.

477
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:10,280
Thanks.

478
00:46:10,800 --> 00:46:14,080
When you're with me, the unlucky things
that happen seem so small.

479
00:46:20,760 --> 00:46:21,680
Come here.

480
00:46:36,160 --> 00:46:37,200
All done.

481
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:42,680
Hey, can I leave my dad's pen with you?

482
00:46:51,920 --> 00:46:52,840
Of course.

483
00:46:55,200 --> 00:46:57,360
I'll take the best care
of your dad for you.

484
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:58,520
I promise.

485
00:47:00,960 --> 00:47:01,840
Thanks.

486
00:47:03,760 --> 00:47:04,600
Hey, wait.

487
00:47:09,760 --> 00:47:10,680
And this…

488
00:47:21,440 --> 00:47:22,840
for good luck.

489
00:47:27,880 --> 00:47:30,520
Thanks. I'm going now.

490
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:34,280
Good luck.

491
00:47:39,560 --> 00:47:41,680
Let's go see how amazing your son is, Dad.

492
00:47:51,560 --> 00:47:53,920
- Am I on time?
- Yeah, but…

493
00:47:55,440 --> 00:47:57,000
What happened to your shirt?

494
00:47:58,760 --> 00:48:00,200
Forget about it.

495
00:48:00,280 --> 00:48:01,760
Is that your shirt?

496
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:03,440
Is that yours?

497
00:48:03,520 --> 00:48:06,800
- Don't worry about it. Just watch him.
- Our final contestant is…

498
00:48:06,880 --> 00:48:08,640
Mr. Khobfa Chaipanha!

499
00:48:30,440 --> 00:48:31,600
You can do it.

500
00:48:34,920 --> 00:48:38,360
This project didn't start with numbers,

501
00:48:39,480 --> 00:48:43,080
not with profit,
not with a business model.

502
00:48:45,240 --> 00:48:47,880
But it started with my dad,

503
00:48:51,840 --> 00:48:55,360
an ordinary man
who has worked his whole life

504
00:48:57,320 --> 00:49:01,320
and yet still doesn't have
a home of his own.

505
00:49:02,080 --> 00:49:04,000
Not because he didn't try,

506
00:49:04,600 --> 00:49:08,400
but because he never had
the same opportunities.

507
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:12,800
So I created HomeStep,

508
00:49:14,480 --> 00:49:18,080
a platform that doesn't only sell homes,

509
00:49:18,160 --> 00:49:23,840
but also helps ordinary people
move closer to owning their homes,

510
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:25,640
step by step.

511
00:49:25,720 --> 00:49:28,000
<i>Don't do it for anyone else.</i>

512
00:49:28,080 --> 00:49:29,440
<i>Just go up there</i>

513
00:49:29,520 --> 00:49:34,040
and imagine you're telling your dad
about your project.

514
00:49:34,640 --> 00:49:35,680
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

515
00:49:35,760 --> 00:49:37,680
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

516
00:49:37,760 --> 00:49:39,440
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

517
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:41,720
<i>Don't let anyone hurt you, okay?</i>

518
00:49:42,720 --> 00:49:44,440
<i>Don't worry about what anyone else says.</i>

519
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:47,480
Just tell them what you want to tell them.

520
00:49:48,080 --> 00:49:49,680
From financial guidance

521
00:49:50,800 --> 00:49:52,120
to building credit

522
00:49:52,720 --> 00:49:56,440
and to finding a home
they can truly afford.

523
00:49:57,320 --> 00:49:58,520
Because in the end,

524
00:49:59,120 --> 00:50:02,160
a home is not just a place to live.

525
00:50:02,240 --> 00:50:04,240
It is stability.

526
00:50:04,960 --> 00:50:09,360
It is the dignity that everyone deserves.

527
00:50:10,160 --> 00:50:11,080
Thank you.

528
00:50:22,160 --> 00:50:24,560
<i>And now, I have the final results</i>
